ance  and when i say you i'm talking about  nba players in general and yet it seems  like  it's groundhog's day where we're seeing  a lot of the same things happen over and  over again how do you keep yourself  motivated and inspired  to keep pushing forward for the kind of  systemic change that you guys want  uh i think for me you know i just think  about our history  you know all the people that came before  us that you know sacrificed their lives  in  a much bigger way that you know myself  and him have opportunities to  to live out our dream and you know that  that doesn't go unnoticed  um and it should be talked about more so  i think we just have to carry that on in  in any way that we can like you said  we're role models  uh more than just basketball players and  um our platform is is huge and you know  it would be  um it'll be wrong if we didn't you know  take advantage of that um the  opportunities that we have  and you know just to speak for all those  people that don't have voices  um like we're doing to share the same  emotions and feelings um that we're  feeling  but we definitely want to express that  it's okay to be upset  it's okay to be angry i think that those  two get confused like we  expressed ourselves through you know  basketball today  winning the game but i mean i think  america has every right to be upset we  don't want to encourage violence  or anything of that nature but you know  we definitely are tired of seeing the  same things  over and over again so you know to feel  that that pain and that emotion  you know you can't control how that  necessarily  um is put out but um we want to continue  to use our platform  because we obviously you know want to  keep inspiring change you know and i  want to believe that  we're doing the right thing

